</span></span></span></p>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="A2.T5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation study comparing LLaMA initialization vs. random initialization.<span id="A2.T5.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Except for CIDEr, using LLaMA as initialization generally offers benefits, especially for dense prompt image generation (DPG) and for VQA performance. Image generation metrics use CFG=3, and VQA results are averaged across benchmarks.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Sampling Steps on Caption Performance</h3>

<figure id="A2.F18" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03506v1/sampling_steps_plot.svg" id="A2.F18.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/118;" width="476" height="118"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F18.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 18</span>: </span><span id="A2.F18.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Performance vs. sampling steps compared to AR.<span id="A2.F18.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> OneFlow achieves parity with the AR model using only 6 sampling steps.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>OneFlow Architecture</h2>

<figure id="A3.F19" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.03506v1/OneFlow.png" id="A3.F19.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/229;" width="381" height="229" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F19.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 19</span>: </span><span id="A3.F19.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Architecture.<span id="A3.F19.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> With a multimodal prompt, OneFlow can produce variable length generations with interleaved text &amp; images in a unified non-autoregressive sequence model, simultaneously generating all modalities with an interleaved time schedule for each generated image and text.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Full Derivations</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide the derivations of the model here. We briefly summarize the Edit Flow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Havasi et al., 2025</a>)</cite> formulation and derivation, and then derive the interleaved time schedule when insertions and image denoising are performed simultaneously.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We make use of a blank token <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote empty spaces within a sequence. This token is only used for tracking token deletions during training and is not part of the vocabulary. Let <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}=\bigcup_{n=0}^{N}({\mathcal{T}}\cup\{{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}\})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}=\bigcup_{n=0}^{N}({\mathcal{T}}\cup\{{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}\})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be an extended space of aligned sequences. Furthermore, define <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{rm-blanks}}:\mathcal{Z}\rightarrow\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>rm-blanks</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{rm-blanks}}:\mathcal{Z}\rightarrow\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> as the function that removes all blank tokens from the sequence. Lastly, we define the delta function over sequences <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z_{1}}(z_{2})=\prod_{i}\delta_{z_{1}^{i}}(z_{2}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z_{1}}(z_{2})=\prod_{i}\delta_{z_{1}^{i}}(z_{2}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math> which is one if all tokens are the same otherwise zero (i.e. Kronecker’s delta function).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Continuous-time Markov chain (CTMC).</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A CTMC is a continuous-time discrete-space process which iteratively jumps between discrete values, with transitions</p>
<table id="A4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(X_{t+h}|X_{t})=\delta_{X_{t}}(X_{t+h})+hu_{t}(x|X_{t})+o(h)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(X_{t+h}|X_{t})=\delta_{X_{t}}(X_{t+h})+hu_{t}(x|X_{t})+o(h),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can be interpreted as a first-order characterization of the transition kernel.
Since with insertions, the sequence lengths of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can change over time. To simplify notation, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Havasi et al. (2025)</a></cite> used an augmented space of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{t},Z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{t},Z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, where it is basically always enforced that <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}=f_{\text{rm-blanks}}(Z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>rm-blanks</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}=f_{\text{rm-blanks}}(Z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. The role of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is only for training, to keep track of which tokens are deleted and to compute the loss, and it is neither seen by the model nor used during sampling.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To briefly summarize the construction below, the Flow Matching recipe makes use of a prescribed conditional CTMC that generates single data sequences, which is then marginalized over the data distribution. The resulting marginal CTMC will then sample from the data distribution.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conditional probability path.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a data sequence <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}\sim p_{\text{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}\sim p_{\text{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we prescribe a conditional probability path over <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of the same sequence length which interpolates between the empty sequence and this data sequence. We then obtain <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by applying the <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{rm-blanks}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>rm-blanks</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{rm-blanks}}</annotation></semantics></math> function. Concretely, we can express the conditional probability path as</p>
<table id="A4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{t}(X_{t},Z_{t}|X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{t}(X_{t},Z_{t}|X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{t}(X_{t}|Z_{t},X_{1})\cdot p_{t}(Z_{t}|X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{t}(X_{t}|Z_{t},X_{1})\cdot p_{t}(Z_{t}|X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{t}(X_{t}|Z_{t})\cdot p_{t}(Z_{t}|Z_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{t}(X_{t}|Z_{t})\cdot p_{t}(Z_{t}|Z_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta_{f_{\text{rm-blanks}}(Z_{t})}(X_{t})\cdot\left(\prod_{i=1}^{n}(1-\kappa_{t})\delta_{{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}}(Z_{t}^{i})+\kappa_{t}\delta_{X_{1}^{i}}(Z_{t}^{i})\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>rm-blanks</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta_{f_{\text{rm-blanks}}(Z_{t})}(X_{t})\cdot\left(\prod_{i=1}^{n}(1-\kappa_{t})\delta_{{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}}(Z_{t}^{i})+\kappa_{t}\delta_{X_{1}^{i}}(Z_{t}^{i})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a scheduler where <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{0}=0,\kappa_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{0}=0,\kappa_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the sequence length of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. In English, (<a href="#A4.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ Conditional probability path. ‣ Appendix D Full Derivations ‣ OneFlow: Concurrent Mixed-Modal and Interleaved Generation with Edit Flows" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) is a mixture distribution where each token <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can either be equal to <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\kappa_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\kappa_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> or equal to data value <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conditional CTMC rate.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Havasi et al. (2025)</a></cite>, a conditional CTMC that samples from this conditional probability path can be constructed as</p>
<table id="A4.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;u_{t}(x,z|X_{t},Z_{t},X_{1})=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}(\delta_{X_{1}^{i}}(z^{i})-\delta_{Z_{t}^{i}}(z^{i}))\right)\delta_{f_{\text{rm-blanks}}(z)}(x),\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\text{ where }x={{\text{ins}}}(X_{t},i,a)\text{ for some $i\in[n]$ and $a\in[M]$}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>rm-blanks</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>ins</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext> for some </mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mtext> and </mtext><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;u_{t}(x,z|X_{t},Z_{t},X_{1})=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}(\delta_{X_{1}^{i}}(z^{i})-\delta_{Z_{t}^{i}}(z^{i}))\right)\delta_{f_{\text{rm-blanks}}(z)}(x),\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\text{ where }x={{\text{ins}}}(X_{t},i,a)\text{ for some $i\in[n]$ and $a\in[M]$}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which denotes the infinitesimal change in probability of going from the state <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{t},Z_{t})\rightarrow(x,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{t},Z_{t})\rightarrow(x,z)</annotation></semantics></math>, constrained to next sequences <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> that are one token insertion difference from <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. In English, (<a href="#A4.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Conditional CTMC rate. ‣ Appendix D Full Derivations ‣ OneFlow: Concurrent Mixed-Modal and Interleaved Generation with Edit Flows" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) assigns a rate of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is not yet equal to <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise, it is zero. This ensures that a sample starting with all blanks <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{0}=[{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon},...{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{0}=[{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon},...{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}]</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> will eventually turn into <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
This ratio <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the infinitesimal rate that each token changes its value, matching the distribution imposed by the scheduler <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and conditioned on that it is still the <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> token at time <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F20" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03506v1/training_figure.svg" id="A4.F20.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/230;" width="333" height="230"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F20.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 20</span>: </span><span id="A4.F20.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">During training we construct <math id="A4.F20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by replacing tokens with the blank token (<math id="A4.F20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>), with the original tokens used to construct the target bag-of-tokens <math id="A4.F20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training loss.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to train a model thats transport sequences via insertions,</p>
<table id="A4.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}^{\theta}(x|X_{t}),\quad\text{ where }x={{\text{ins}}}(X_{t},i,a)\text{ for some $i$ and $a$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>ins</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext> for some </mtext><mi>i</mi><mtext> and </mtext><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}^{\theta}(x|X_{t}),\quad\text{ where }x={{\text{ins}}}(X_{t},i,a)\text{ for some $i$ and $a$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">we would need to marginalize out the auxiliary process <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and the data <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Havasi et al. (2025)</a></cite> showed this can be done by using a loss based on any Bregman divergence while summing up over all possible sequences <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=f_{\text{rm-blanks}}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>rm-blanks</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=f_{\text{rm-blanks}}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>. Concretely, given a convex function <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> that defines a Bregman divergence <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\phi}(a,b)=\phi(a)-\phi(b)-\langle a-b,\tfrac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}b}\phi(b)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\phi}(a,b)=\phi(a)-\phi(b)-\langle a-b,\tfrac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}b}\phi(b)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, we can use the loss</p>
<table id="A4.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{X_{t},Z_{t}\sim p_{t}(X_{t},Z_{t}|X_{1}),X_{1}\sim p_{\text{data}}}D_{\phi}\Big(\textstyle\sum_{z}u_{t}(\cdot,z|X_{t},Z_{t},X_{1}),u_{t}^{\theta}(\cdot|X_{t})\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>z</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{X_{t},Z_{t}\sim p_{t}(X_{t},Z_{t}|X_{1}),X_{1}\sim p_{\text{data}}}D_{\phi}\Big(\textstyle\sum_{z}u_{t}(\cdot,z|X_{t},Z_{t},X_{1}),u_{t}^{\theta}(\cdot|X_{t})\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Plugging in the entropy <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(u)=\langle u,\log u\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(u)=\langle u,\log u\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, this results in the Edit Flow loss</p>
<table id="A4.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{t,p_{t}(X_{t},Z_{t}|X_{1}),X_{1}\sim p_{\text{data}}}\left[\sum_{x\neq X_{t}}u_{t}^{\theta}(x|X_{t})-\sum_{i=1}^{n}\bm{1}_{[Z_{t}^{i}={\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}]}\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}\log u_{t}^{\theta}({{\text{ins}}}(X_{t},j,X_{1}^{i})|X_{t})\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi>log</mi><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>ins</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{t,p_{t}(X_{t},Z_{t}|X_{1}),X_{1}\sim p_{\text{data}}}\left[\sum_{x\neq X_{t}}u_{t}^{\theta}(x|X_{t})-\sum_{i=1}^{n}\bm{1}_{[Z_{t}^{i}={\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}]}\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}\log u_{t}^{\theta}({{\text{ins}}}(X_{t},j,X_{1}^{i})|X_{t})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is the position in <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> that corresponds to the first non-<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> token on the left of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. This ensures that inserting at the <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th position corresponds to changing the value of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Loss simplification.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We deviate from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Havasi et al. (2025)</a></cite> and use a <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-independent parameterization. In particular, for sequences <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> that are one token insertion of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x={{\text{ins}}}(X_{t},i,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>ins</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x={{\text{ins}}}(X_{t},i,a)</annotation></semantics></math>, we use</p>
<table id="A4.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}^{\theta}\big({{\text{ins}}}(X_{t},i,a)|X_{t}\big)=\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}\lambda^{i}(X_{t})Q^{i}(a|X_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mtext>ins</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}^{\theta}\big({{\text{ins}}}(X_{t},i,a)|X_{t}\big)=\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}\lambda^{i}(X_{t})Q^{i}(a|X_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the neural network parameterizes <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using this parameterization, letting <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of missing tokens to the right of position <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the training loss (<a href="#A4.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ Training loss. ‣ Appendix D Full Derivations ‣ OneFlow: Concurrent Mixed-Modal and Interleaved Generation with Edit Flows" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) can be decomposed into</p>
<table id="A4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{(\dots)}\left(\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}\right)\Bigg(\sum_{j=1}^{n(X_{t})}\lambda^{j}(X_{t})-\sum_{j=1}^{n(X_{t})}\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{j}}\log\left(\lambda^{j}(X_{t})Q^{j}(a|X_{t})\right)\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{(\dots)}\left(\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}\right)\Bigg(\sum_{j=1}^{n(X_{t})}\lambda^{j}(X_{t})-\sum_{j=1}^{n(X_{t})}\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{j}}\log\left(\lambda^{j}(X_{t})Q^{j}(a|X_{t})\right)\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{(\dots)}\left(\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}\right)\sum_{j=1}^{n(X_{t})}\Bigg(\underbrace{\vphantom{\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{j}}}\lambda^{j}(X_{t})-|\mathcal{A}_{i}|\log\lambda^{j}(X_{t})}_{(\ref{eq:poisson_nll})}+\underbrace{\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{j}}\log Q^{j}(a|X_{t})}_{(\ref{eq:token_loss})}\Bigg)+\text{const.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S2.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 2.1.2 Insertion prediction (𝜆^𝑖). ‣ 2.1 Discrete Text Generation via Edit Flows ‣ 2 OneFlow: Mixed-Modal Generation through Flow Matching ‣ OneFlow: Concurrent Mixed-Modal and Interleaved Generation with Edit Flows" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 2.1.3 Bag-of-tokens prediction (𝑄^𝑖). ‣ 2.1 Discrete Text Generation via Edit Flows ‣ 2 OneFlow: Mixed-Modal Generation through Flow Matching ‣ OneFlow: Concurrent Mixed-Modal and Interleaved Generation with Edit Flows" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mtext>const.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{(\dots)}\left(\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}\right)\sum_{j=1}^{n(X_{t})}\Bigg(\underbrace{\vphantom{\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{j}}}\lambda^{j}(X_{t})-|\mathcal{A}_{i}|\log\lambda^{j}(X_{t})}_{(\ref{eq:poisson_nll})}+\underbrace{\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{j}}\log Q^{j}(a|X_{t})}_{(\ref{eq:token_loss})}\Bigg)+\text{const.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which recovers the losses for <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 2.1.2 Insertion prediction (𝜆^𝑖). ‣ 2.1 Discrete Text Generation via Edit Flows ‣ 2 OneFlow: Mixed-Modal Generation through Flow Matching ‣ OneFlow: Concurrent Mixed-Modal and Interleaved Generation with Edit Flows" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 2.1.3 Bag-of-tokens prediction (𝑄^𝑖). ‣ 2.1 Discrete Text Generation via Edit Flows ‣ 2 OneFlow: Mixed-Modal Generation through Flow Matching ‣ OneFlow: Concurrent Mixed-Modal and Interleaved Generation with Edit Flows" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) respectively, after removing the coefficient <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\dot{\kappa}_{t}}{1-\kappa_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>. While keeping this coefficient relates the loss the to an evidence lower bound <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Havasi et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, we found that removing this coefficient in the loss gave better results in practice.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Interleaved time schedule</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to model image insertions, we would make a choice. We can either (i) fully denoise images at the time of insertion, or (ii) insert only noise and denoise later. We choose the latter approach, as this allows simultaneous generation across images and text, and provides the best parallelism as only a single model forward at each step is needed for both modalities. Without loss of generality, assume there is only a single image.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Generation starts by advancing the sequence time, denoted <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{text}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{text}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. When the image is inserted, we associate the image with its own time <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{img}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{img}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The main difficulty is that we can not simply set <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{img}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{img}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{text}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{text}}</annotation></semantics></math> independently during training, as evidently we always have <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{text}}\geq t_{\text{img}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{text}}\geq t_{\text{img}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In fact, an independent scheduler induces the wrong distribution for our insertion prediction, and it will not insert the correct distribution at generation time. Instead, we need to ensure that training and generation see the same distribution of time values. To achieve this, we first note that the image exists in the sequence according to the scheduler <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, which means that the <em id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">insertion times</em> are distributed according to</p>
<table id="A4.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t_{\text{insert}})=\dot{\kappa}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>insert</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t_{\text{insert}})=\dot{\kappa}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{insert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>insert</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{insert}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the time at which an image is inserted, <span id="A4.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cumulative distribution function (CDF) of the insertion times. Equivalently, to sample the insertion time, we can apply the inverse CDF sampling,</p>
<table id="A4.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{insert}}=\kappa^{-1}(u),\qquad u\sim\text{Unif}(0,1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>insert</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Unif</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{insert}}=\kappa^{-1}(u),\qquad u\sim\text{Unif}(0,1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">If we set <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{img}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{img}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> when an image is inserted, then the difference between <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{text}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{text}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{img}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{img}}</annotation></semantics></math> is distributed according to the insertion time. This gives us the relation</p>
<table id="A4.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{text}}-t_{\text{img}}=t_{\text{insert}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>insert</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{text}}-t_{\text{img}}=t_{\text{insert}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">when <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq t_{\text{text}},t_{\text{img}},t_{\text{insert}}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>insert</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq t_{\text{text}},t_{\text{img}},t_{\text{insert}}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{text}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{text}}</annotation></semantics></math> will reach 1 before <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{img}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{img}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we want to train for the entire process until <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{img}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{img}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we can construct an extended time interval</p>
<table id="A4.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{text}}\in[0,2],\qquad t_{\text{text}}=\text{clip}(\tau_{\text{text}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>clip</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{text}}\in[0,2],\qquad t_{\text{text}}=\text{clip}(\tau_{\text{text}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{clip}(\tau)=\min\{1,\max\{0,\tau\}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>clip</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{clip}(\tau)=\min\{1,\max\{0,\tau\}\}</annotation></semantics></math> clips the time values back into the interval <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">During training, we first sample <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{text}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{text}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then sample</p>
<table id="A4.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{img}}=\tau_{\text{text}}-\kappa^{-1}(u),\qquad u\sim\text{Unif}(0,1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Unif</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{img}}=\tau_{\text{text}}-\kappa^{-1}(u),\qquad u\sim\text{Unif}(0,1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">This will sample an extended time for the image in the internal [-1, 2]. If <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{img}}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{img}}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then it has not yet been inserted, hence it is deleted from the sequence. Otherwise, it is clip,</p>
<table id="A4.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{img}}=\text{clip}(\tau_{\text{img}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>clip</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{img}}=\text{clip}(\tau_{\text{img}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">and we proceed to use the Flow Matching loss (<a href="#S2.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ 2.2 Continuous Image Generation via Flow Matching ‣ 2 OneFlow: Mixed-Modal Generation through Flow Matching ‣ OneFlow: Concurrent Mixed-Modal and Interleaved Generation with Edit Flows" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) to train the image denoising.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Sampling and Training Algorithms</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OneFlow interleaved text–image generation.</span></figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span> <span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OneFlowGeneration</span>(step size <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>, schedule <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> empty sequence <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="alg1.l2.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Text tokens (initially empty set)</em>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="alg1.l3.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Set of image latents with per-image times</em>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{text}}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{text}}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{text}}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{text}}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">or</span> <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists Y\in\mathcal{I}:t_{\text{img}}(Y)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists Y\in\mathcal{I}:t_{\text{img}}(Y)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,\mathcal{I},t_{\text{text}},t_{\text{img}}\leftarrow\textsc{OneFlowStep}(X,\mathcal{I},t_{\text{text}},t_{\text{img}},\Delta t,\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">OneFlowStep</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>text</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,\mathcal{I},t_{\text{text}},t_{\text{img}}\leftarrow\textsc{OneFlowStep}(X,\mathcal{I},t_{\text{text}},t_{\text{img}},\Delta t,\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\text{VAEDec}(Y):Y\in\mathcal{I}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>VAEDec</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\text{VAEDec}(Y):Y\in\mathcal{I}\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="alg1.l8.4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Decode VAE latents into image space</em>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> <span id="alg2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OneFlow step function.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="alg2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is the token sequence, <math id="alg2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of image latents each with time <math id="alg2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{img}}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{img}}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
